{"name":"Ballerina Tutu","hex":"#c8647f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ballerina","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ballet dancer \n A female ballet dancer.\nEllipsis of prima ballerina (“the star female ballet performer in the company”).","A female ballet dancer.\nEllipsis of prima ballerina (“the star female ballet performer in the company”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballerina"},{"term":"tutu","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ballet skirt made of layered stiff but light netting."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain members of genus Coriaria of shrubs and trees found in New Zealand, including Coriaria arborea and Coriaria pottsiana, used by the Maori to make a sweetener, but toxic when not properly prepared."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tutu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tutu (clothing)","blocks":[{"text":"A tutu is a dress worn as a costume in a classical ballet performance, often with attached bodice. It may be made of tarlatan, muslin, silk, tulle, gauze, or nylon. Modern tutus have two basic types: the Romantic tutu is soft and bell-shaped, reaching the calf or ankle; the Classical tutu is short and stiff, projecting horizontally from the waist and hip."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Colourful_ballet_tutu.jpg/330px-Colourful_ballet_tutu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tutu_(clothing)","wikidata":"Q1359804"},{"title":"Ballet dancer","blocks":[{"text":"A ballet dancer is a person who practices the art of classical ballet. Both women and men can practice ballet. They rely on years of extensive training and proper technique to become a part of a professional ballet company. Ballet dancers are at a high risk of injury due to the demanding technique of ballet dancing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Corsaire_